f <!-- -->4</p><div class="page_heroTags__X4Aum"><span class="page_heroTag__nwSAc">How-To</span><span class="page_heroTag__nwSAc">Permits</span><span class="page_heroTag__nwSAc">Regulations</span><span class="page_heroTag__nwSAc">Miami</span><span class="page_heroTag__nwSAc">Miami-Dade County</span></div></div><div class="page_heroImageWrapper__boqRT"><img alt="Complete guide to site work permits in Miami and Miami-Dade County" fetchPriority="high" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="page_heroImage__Amcvu" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="/images/services/site-work-development.png"/></div></div></div></section><section class="page_section__dDgCF"><div class="page_container___eH_v"><div class="page_contentLayout__L4LPb"><article class="page_article__9txy5"><div class="page_mobileTOCWrapper__EUAOS"><div class="ResourceTOC_mobileTOC___bb5Q"><button class="ResourceTOC_mobileToggle__GCAiK" aria-expanded="false"><span>Contents</span><span class="ResourceTOC_toggleIcon__5wyoh">+</span></button></div><nav class="ResourceTOC_desktopTOC__yqJxF" aria-label="Table of contents"><h2 class="ResourceTOC_tocTitle__HdVdr">Table of contents</h2><ul class="ResourceTOC_tocList__4cY2p"><li><a href="#introduction" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">Understanding Site Work Permits in Miami-Dade County</a></li><li><a href="#permit-overview" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">Overview of Site Work Permits Required in Miami-Dade</a></li><li><a href="#miami-building-permits" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">Miami-Dade County Building Department Permits</a><ul class="ResourceTOC_tocSubList__gI4Ir"><li><a href="#building-permit-requirements" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ResourceTOC_tocSubLink__LwB4t ">Building Department Permit Requirements</a></li><li><a href="#required-documents" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ResourceTOC_tocSubLink__LwB4t ">Required Documents for Building Permits</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="#derm-permits" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">Miami-Dade DERM Permits</a><ul class="ResourceTOC_tocSubList__gI4Ir"><li><a href="#derm-permit-requirements" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ResourceTOC_tocSubLink__LwB4t ">DERM Permit Requirements</a></li><li><a href="#derm-review-process" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ResourceTOC_tocSubLink__LwB4t ">DERM Review Process</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="#dtpw-requirements" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">Miami-Dade DTPW Requirements</a><ul class="ResourceTOC_tocSubList__gI4Ir"><li><a href="#dtpw-permit-requirements" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ResourceTOC_tocSubLink__LwB4t ">DTPW Permit Requirements</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="#sfwmd-permits" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">South Florida Water Management District Permits</a></li><li><a href="#tree-removal-permits" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">Tree Removal and Vegetation Permits in Miami-Dade</a><ul class="ResourceTOC_tocSubList__gI4Ir"><li><a href="#tree-permit-requirements" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ResourceTOC_tocSubLink__LwB4t ">Tree Removal Permit Requirements</a></li><li><a href="#miami-tree-ordinances" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ResourceTOC_tocSubLink__LwB4t ">Miami-Dade Tree Protection Ordinances</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="#flood-zone-requirements" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">Flood Zone Requirements in Miami-Dade</a><ul class="ResourceTOC_tocSubList__gI4Ir"><li><a href="#flood-zone-permits" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ResourceTOC_tocSubLink__LwB4t ">Flood Zone Permit Requirements</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="#permit-application-process" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">How to Apply for Site Work Permits in Miami-Dade</a><ul class="ResourceTOC_tocSubList__gI4Ir"><li><a href="#pre-application" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ResourceTOC_tocSubLink__LwB4t ">Pre-Application Phase</a></li><li><a href="#application-submission" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ResourceTOC_tocSubLink__LwB4t ">Application Submission</a></li><li><a href="#review-process" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ResourceTOC_tocSubLink__LwB4t ">Review and Approval Process</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="#common-permit-mistakes" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">Common Permit Mistakes to Avoid in Miami</a></li><li><a href="#permit-costs" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">Permit Costs and Fees in Miami-Dade</a></li><li><a href="#working-with-contractors" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">Working with Contractors on Permits in Miami</a></li><li><a href="#conclusion" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">Conclusion</a></li></ul></nav></div><div id="introduction" class="page_section__dDgCF"><h2 class="page_h2___8XA5">Understanding Site Work Permits in Miami-Dade County</h2><div class="page_paragraph__Jg7TY">Obtaining the necessary permits is one of the most critical and often challenging aspects of site work in Miami-Dade County. The county has some of the strictest permitting requirements in Florida, with multiple agencies involved in the approval process including <a href="https://www.miamidade.gov/global/service.page?Mduid_service=ser1462287521891415" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Miami-Dade DERM</a>, the Building Department, and <a href="https://www.miamidade.gov/global/service.page?Mduid_service=ser1462287521891415" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">DTPW</a>.</div><p class="page_paragraph__Jg7TY">This comprehensive guide walks you through the permit process for site work in Miami-Dade County. Understanding what permits you need, how to apply, and what to expect helps ensure your project proceeds without delays. Whether you&#x27;re working in Miami, Miami Beach, Coral Gables, Aventura, or throughout the county, this guide provides the information you need.</p><p class="page_paragraph__Jg7TY">Working without proper permits can result in stop-work orders, fines, and project delays. Taking time to understand and obtain all required permits upfront saves time and money in the long run.</p></div><div id="permit-overview" class="page_section__dDgCF"><h2 class="page_h2___8XA5">Overview of Site Work Permits Required in Miami-Dade</h2><div class="page_sectionImageWrapper__WJRPB"><img alt="Site work permits and regulatory requirements in Miami-Dade County" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="page_sectionImage__3DB3n" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="/images/services/site-work-development.png"/></div><p class="page_paragraph__Jg7TY">Most site work projects in Miami-Dade County require multiple permits from different agencies. Here&#x27;s an overview of the main permit categories:</p><div class="page_paragraph__Jg7TY"><ul><li><strong>Building Department Permits:</strong> Required for most site work activities including grading, excavation, and drainage</li><li><strong>DERM Permits:</strong> Required for projects affecting water resources, wetlands, protected species, or environmental features</li><li><strong>Tree Removal Permits:</strong> Required before removing trees or vegetation (issued by DERM)</li><li><strong>Utility Permits:</strong> Required for work affecting or installing utilities</li><li><strong>DTPW Permits:</strong> Required for work in public rights-of-way</li><li><strong>Flood Zone Permits:</strong> Special requirements for properties in flood zones (many Miami-Dade properties are in Zone AE or VE)</li></ul></div><p class="page_paragraph__Jg7TY">The specific permits required depend on your project type, location, and scope of work. Coastal areas like Miami Beach and Key Biscayne face additional environmental requirements.</p><section class="CTABanner_banner__WEwnA"><div class="CTABanner_container__R7oCZ"><div class="CTABanner_content__2ACRq"><h2 class="CTABanner_title__vxPaY">Need Help with Site Work Permits in Miami?</h2><p class="CTABanner_description__L5DsY">Get expert guidance on permit requirements for your project in Miami-Dade County. Our network of licensed contractors understands Miami&#x27;s complex permit process and can help ensure compliance.</p><div class="CTABanner_actions__iTyv4"><a class="CTABanner_primaryButton__DBoqD" href="/contact/">Get Free Quote</a></div></div></div></section></div><div id="miami-building-permits" class="page_section__dDgCF"><h2 class="page_h2___8XA5">Miami-Dade County Building Department Permits</h2><div class="page_sectionImageWrapper__WJRPB"><img alt="Miami-Dade County Building Department site work permits" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" class="page_sectionImage__3DB3n" style="position:absolute;height:100%;width:100%;left:0;top:0;right:0;bottom:0;color:transparent" src="/images/services/commercial-site-work.jpg"/></div><div class="page_paragraph__Jg7TY">The <a href="https://www.miamidade.gov/global/service.page?Mduid_service=ser1462287521891415" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Miami-Dade Building Department</a> requires permits for most site work activities. Understanding these requirements is essential for successful projects in Miami, Miami Beach, Coral Gables, and throughout the county.</div><div id="building-permit-requirements" class="page_subsection__Wu9WH"><h3 class="page_h3__9IITG">Building Department Permit Requirements</h3><p class="page_paragraph__Jg7TY">The Miami-Dade Building Department requires permits for:</p><div class="page_paragraph__Jg7TY"><ul><li>Site grading and earthwork</li><li>Excavation for foundations and utilities</li><li>Drainage system installation</li><li>Utility installation and connections</li><li>Erosion control measures</li><li>Retention and detention pond construction</li></ul></div><div class="page_paragraph__Jg7TY">Permit applications must include site plans, engineering drawings, stormwater calculations, and erosion control plans. Processing typically takes 30-60 days. Learn about <a href="/service-areas/miami/">Miami site work services</a> and local requirements.</div></div><div id="required-documents" class="page_subsection__Wu9WH"><h3 class="page_h3__9IITG">Required Documents for Building Permits</h3><p class="page_paragraph__Jg7TY">Building permit applications must include:</p><div class="page_paragraph__Jg7TY"><ul><li>Site plans showing existing and proposed conditions</li><li>Engineering drawings with calculations</li><li>Stormwater management plans (must comply with DERM and SFWMD)</li><li>Erosion control plans</li><li>Property surveys</li><li>Flood zone determination (check <a href="https://www.fema.gov/flood-maps" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood maps</a>)</li><li>Utility coordination letters</li></ul></div><p class="page_paragraph__Jg7TY">Incomplete applications are typically rejected, causing delays. Ensure all required documents and fees are included.</p></div></div></article><aside class="page_sidebar__U1sbQ"><div class="ResourceTOC_mobileTOC___bb5Q"><button class="ResourceTOC_mobileToggle__GCAiK" aria-expanded="false"><span>Contents</span><span class="ResourceTOC_toggleIcon__5wyoh">+</span></button></div><nav class="ResourceTOC_desktopTOC__yqJxF" aria-label="Table of contents"><h2 class="ResourceTOC_tocTitle__HdVdr">Table of contents</h2><ul class="ResourceTOC_tocList__4cY2p"><li><a href="#introduction" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">Understanding Site Work Permits in Miami-Dade County</a></li><li><a href="#permit-overview" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">Overview of Site Work Permits Required in Miami-Dade</a></li><li><a href="#miami-building-permits" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ">Miami-Dade County Building Department Permits</a><ul class="ResourceTOC_tocSubList__gI4Ir"><li><a href="#building-permit-requirements" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ResourceTOC_tocSubLink__LwB4t ">Building Department Permit Requirements</a></li><li><a href="#required-documents" class="ResourceTOC_tocLink__mxPJA ResourceTOC_tocSubLink__LwB4t ">Required Documents for Building Permits</a></li></ul></li><li><a href="#der